WEBVTT

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.010
"April 11th - 9:02 AM
1 Day Till Launch"

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:16.510
"Albinar Cosmodrome - Launch Pad"

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:20.640
The flight plan is similar to hers.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:21.600
Right.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.190
After we've confirmed
you're safe in space,

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:32.530
we'll announce the launch was successful
and broadcast its status live.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:41.040
They'll play the transcript on the
evening news. Did you read the notes?

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:47.210
You mean, reporting that I feel fine
during the flight, even if I don't?

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:53.720
Yeah. The old ploy of our motherland:
if something's inconvenient, lie about--

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:56.010
Chief!

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:17.410
"Irina: The Vampire Cosmonaut"

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:32.690
"Lies and Truths"

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:34.980
"April 12th - 7:00 AM
2 Hours Till Launch"

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:36.990
"Albinar Cosmodrome - Rocket Hangar"

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:48.250
How are you feeling, Comrade Leps?

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:49.830
Very relaxed.

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:05.640
U-Um...!

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:06.600
What?

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:10.100
I'm sorry. Could we stop the bus?

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:12.810
What's wrong? Tell me.

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:15.270
Um...

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:16.610
I've gotta pee.

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:28.660
Don't worry us like that, you goon!

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.670
You, too?

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:40.920
I'm not like you.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:46.010
Sorry. You wouldn't make
yourself look like a fool.

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:48.180
--Congrats.
--Huh?

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:55.860
You're the one who can carry people's
dreams and make them smile. It's true.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:57.650
Mikhail...

00:03:57.650 --> 00:04:05.320
If I'd been picked, I would've played
the perfect hero. Forget pissing.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:14.420
To be honest, when you stopped the bus,
I hoped that you suddenly felt sick.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:20.920
What's more, I've been hoping that
you'd find an issue with your space suit.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:26.850
Now I finally understand why
you were chosen and I wasn't.

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:31.640
You'll make everyone's dreams come true.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:37.980
Thanks.

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:43.280
Can you take my dreams to space, too?

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:44.320
Yeah.

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:47.530
"7:50 AM
70 Minutes Till Launch"

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:52.500
To think, they really chose you!

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:54.500
Yustin!

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:57.210
--Sign this one, too!
--Sure.

00:04:57.210 --> 00:04:58.960
Morning!

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:02.090
It's perfect weather for a launch.

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:04.340
Chief! You okay?

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:07.340
Don't worry. I'm managing.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:14.140
Comrade Lev Leps, people have
dreamed of going to space for ages.

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:18.190
Today's the first step
of fulfilling that dream.

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:21.650
What's wrong? Starting to feel nervous?

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:27.320
No.

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:31.160
Take care of Irina
when she joins the Bureau.

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:33.290
Hmm? What do you mean?

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:34.160
Huh?

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:36.500
I've heard nothing of the sort.

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:44.210
I'm transferring--leaving here
and going to Sangrad.

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:49.220
I'll undergo health exams while
working at the Design Bureau.

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:02.730
Was that a lie?

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:07.780
You should get going.
I'll do everything in my power.

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:12.580
Listen, Lev. The space you
yearn for is within grasp.

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:17.830
Your dream is ours...
and her dream as well.

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:22.420
Come back safe, for her sake, too.

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:30.050
Long live cosmonaut Lev Leps!

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:31.850
Long live--

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:36.680
Let's meet again when
you get back from space.

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:40.270
Irina... I know how you feel.

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:44.440
Let's go.

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:49.320
"8:45 AM
15 Minutes Till Launch"

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:03.250
All systems are good to go.
No issues reported.

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:06.460
This is Dawn. Can you hear me, Aster?

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:07.510
I can.

00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:09.720
We're late, but it won't be long.

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:10.720
Roger.

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:34.030
One minute to launch.

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:37.450
Roger. Preparing for launch.

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:38.620
Set keys!

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:40.040
Keys set!

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:41.500
Ignition sequence!

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:46.090
Preliminary stage!

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:50.880
Intermediate stage!

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:55.300
Engine ignition!

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:05.270
Here we go!

00:08:05.270 --> 00:08:06.440
Launch!

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:31.420
Dawn here. Do you copy, Aster?

00:08:31.420 --> 00:08:35.930
Aster here. I feel good.
We're flying steady.

00:08:37.470 --> 00:08:39.310
First stage separation.

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:49.980
Heart rate: 159. Rising to 160!

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:55.740
This is Dawn! Aster, come in!
Aster, come in!

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:02.540
Fairing jettison.

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:16.800
Aster here. I see the surface.

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:17.970
Yes!

00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:29.360
No issues with me or the cabin.

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:30.940
It's beautiful.

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:46.670
Second stage jettison.

00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:48.920
Third stage ignition.

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:05.270
Third stage jettison.

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:09.730
The launch was successful!
The ship is in orbit!

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:14.530
We did it, Comrade Chief.

00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:15.780
Yeah.

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:30.880
What's the point of doing this?

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:33.380
Irina had enough in her log.

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:53.400
Aster here. The cabin is stable
at 60% humidity and 20 degrees.

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:59.280
The planet... I can see
the globe beneath me.

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:01.870
How did the planet look?

00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:08.500
Like it was wrapped in a beautiful,
blue veil. So pretty.

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:13.080
It looks like it's wrapped in a blue veil.

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:28.060
Irina... Here's space through your eyes.

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:34.270
The stars... They're sparkling
like blooming chervil flowers.

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:36.650
The moon...

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:39.820
I can't see the moon from here.

00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:46.240
Um, seeing the moon in space
made me realize something...

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:47.740
And that's...

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:56.630
Aster here.

00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:08.520
Let's celebrate this great
achievement with <i>kholodets</i>,

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:10.480
while giving all our thanks.

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:15.610
"Sangrad - Glorious Square"

00:12:15.610 --> 00:12:19.360
"Sangrad - Glorious Square"
Notice from Sangrad! Notice from Sangrad!

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:25.820
On April 12th, 1961,
the UZSR spacecraft "Mechta"

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:29.700
has gone to space with a human on board!

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:35.000
The cosmonaut is Major Lev Leps
from the Zirnitra Union!

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:41.550
I repeat, the cosmonaut is Major Lev Leps
from the Zirnitra Union!

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:45.090
Our motherland,
wielding the power of science,

00:12:45.090 --> 00:12:48.760
has opened the era of space conquest!

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:51.850
--Hurrah!
--Hurrah!
--They did it!

00:12:56.690 --> 00:12:58.020
Huh?

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:05.360
Zirnitra, hurrah! Major Lev Leps, hurrah!

00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:10.160
I-It launched!

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:13.580
--Huh?
--Lev is flying through space!

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:15.670
He is?! Huh?

00:13:18.670 --> 00:13:19.920
Irina!

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:27.140
Lev is in space!

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:32.970
He says that our planet looks
to be wrapped in a blue veil!

00:13:32.970 --> 00:13:36.190
What? That's what I said!

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:40.440
And the stars look like
blooming chervil flowers!

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:43.440
I said that, too!

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:46.070
You didn't even know what a chervil was!

00:13:49.740 --> 00:13:55.410
Zirnitra, hurrah! Major Lev Leps, hurrah!

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:58.460
Zirnitra, hurrah! Major Lev Leps, hurrah!

00:13:58.460 --> 00:13:59.960
Lev?

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:16.020
Why? Is it because I'm a vampire?

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:20.440
Lev, why did you use my words?

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:25.360
Also, he wanted to share
this message with everyone:

00:14:27.320 --> 00:14:30.320
Answer me, Lev!

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:34.540
"Let's celebrate this great
achievement with <i>kholodets</i>,

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:37.370
while giving all our thanks."

00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:46.170
Irina!

00:14:54.560 --> 00:15:00.480
<i>Kholodets</i>... That's a message
from Lev to you, isn't it?

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:01.810
Mmm.

00:15:01.810 --> 00:15:05.730
It's painful, no? It's sad, no?

00:15:05.730 --> 00:15:11.450
That this is the only way anyone
will know what you've done.

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:16.240
But, I know! Lev knows, too!

00:15:16.240 --> 00:15:21.420
We know how hard you worked for it!
We know the feelings you put into it!

00:15:48.990 --> 00:15:50.990
"Palma Plains"

00:15:57.540 --> 00:16:00.120
My dear comrade, Lev Leps.

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:05.380
It's an honor to speak with you,
who took our motherland to space.

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:10.420
"Zirnitra Union
Air Force Base"
It's thanks to my comrades
that the flight was successful.

00:16:10.420 --> 00:16:16.300
Comrade Leps, being the first
human to ever fly in space,

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:20.930
your name will be immortalized in history.

00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:22.940
There's no greater honor.

00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:28.320
Now then, I'll take you to your lodgings.

00:16:28.650 --> 00:16:30.650
"April 13th - 11:30 AM"

00:16:30.650 --> 00:16:32.650
"A Southwestern Republic of UZSR
City of Borshev"

00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:33.610
"Newspaper 'The Istina'
World's First Cosmonaut"

00:16:33.610 --> 00:16:36.620
"Newspaper 'The Istina'
World's First Cosmonaut"
The world's first cosmonaut, huh?

00:16:41.710 --> 00:16:47.250
It's time for work, Mr. Hero.
Do try to be friendly.

00:16:52.590 --> 00:16:54.720
--Major Leps!
--Can I have a word?

00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:58.510
--What was the flight like?
--Can you tell us anything more?

00:17:02.770 --> 00:17:06.230
You were here? You should've said so.

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:08.730
Well done coming home.

00:17:08.730 --> 00:17:16.450
Allow me to thank you, Private Lev--
Major. Congrats on the promotion.

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:18.990
Thank you.

00:17:18.990 --> 00:17:21.120
Hmm? What's wrong?

00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:25.580
If you're tired already, you won't
last tomorrow's celebration.

00:17:25.580 --> 00:17:26.960
It's the newspaper.

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:28.420
Hmm?

00:17:28.420 --> 00:17:31.050
Your name wasn't mentioned in it.

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:37.760
That's all you're worried about?

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:44.060
I don't mind. If I thought it'd help our
budget, I'd print my face everywhere.

00:17:44.060 --> 00:17:45.890
--Also...
--Hmm?

00:17:45.890 --> 00:17:49.060
The reason I was able to come home safe--

00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:51.440
Is thanks to Lycoris.

00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:57.410
You seem concerned about her, Aster.

00:17:59.070 --> 00:18:03.620
I intend to do all I can,
but I make no promises.

00:18:03.620 --> 00:18:09.960
I told you at the start: you're
expected to set aside everything.

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:14.260
Do you know why I
recommended you as cosmonaut?

00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:15.260
No.

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:22.640
Because I believed you had the resolve
to lead the world into a new age.

00:18:22.640 --> 00:18:24.220
Resolve, huh?

00:18:24.220 --> 00:18:26.350
Nope, zero points.

00:18:26.350 --> 00:18:31.980
Not enough gratitude to our
motherland or leader. Do it again.

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:35.530
It seems like your head is in the clouds.

00:18:35.530 --> 00:18:39.610
Thinking about our cute
experiment subject, perhaps?

00:18:39.610 --> 00:18:43.120
Aren't you forgetting
to treat her like an object?

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:49.040
Irina. What will happen to her?

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:55.130
We dispose of things we don't need.
That's how our country works.

00:18:56.210 --> 00:18:59.470
After yesterday, your life changed.

00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:04.010
Delicious.

00:19:04.010 --> 00:19:11.230
Now you carry the responsibility
of being the first cosmonaut in history.

00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:15.190
You should've known
it wouldn't always be pleasant.

00:19:15.190 --> 00:19:20.110
Say, do you remember what
I looked for in a cosmonaut?

00:19:20.110 --> 00:19:23.580
A revolutionary who would
lead us to the new world.

00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:30.420
Yes. Having gone to the new world
of space, you could lead the people.

00:19:30.420 --> 00:19:33.670
You have the power to cause a revolution.

00:19:33.670 --> 00:19:37.210
You can drink in the
sweet-as-chocolate praise,

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:40.550
or feed them a poison, like lycoris.

00:19:43.180 --> 00:19:46.100
Do hurry up with your speech.

00:19:52.810 --> 00:19:55.440
Revolution? Gimme a break.

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:14.790
We've received orders from him.
It's to happen at 3 PM tomorrow.

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:19.960
Comrade Chief...
This is a threat masked as a plea.

00:20:23.470 --> 00:20:24.720
What is it?

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:27.180
Preparation is complete.

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:32.020
Tomorrow will go down in history.

00:20:32.020 --> 00:20:39.480
Indeed. People will--
No, the world shall remember it forever.

00:20:44.910 --> 00:20:46.870
"Sangrad"

00:20:46.990 --> 00:20:49.830
Long live the motherland!

00:20:54.580 --> 00:21:01.510
I have new orders. After tomorrow,
I'm not assigned to you anymore.

00:21:01.510 --> 00:21:02.920
Huh?

00:21:02.920 --> 00:21:08.390
It was only supposed to last
till the manned launch.

00:21:08.390 --> 00:21:09.890
I see.

00:21:14.850 --> 00:21:20.190
Anya, could you do me a favor?

00:21:20.190 --> 00:21:24.360
Give this to Lev and tell him "Congrats."

00:21:24.360 --> 00:21:27.070
That's...

00:21:27.070 --> 00:21:29.120
Give it to him yourself!

00:21:29.120 --> 00:21:31.790
But, I...

00:21:33.660 --> 00:21:39.090
Giving up doesn't suit the person
who opened the path to space!

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:43.300
Don't you wanna see Lev?!

00:21:45.800 --> 00:21:49.600
I do! I wanna talk to him!

00:21:51.100 --> 00:21:58.560
All right. I'm very angry right now--at
this country where one can't love freely!

00:21:58.560 --> 00:21:59.940
Anya...

00:23:48.260 --> 00:23:51.010
"Next Episode:
'To the New World'"
